<title>USA: K-III's Films for the Humanities names COO.</title>
<headline>K-III's Films for the Humanities names COO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>K-III Communications' Films for the Humanities and Sciences, a distributor of videos and CD-ROMs, named Betsy Sherer as chief operating officer. Sherer replaces Michael Mantell who resigned.</p>
<p>Previously, Sherer served as vice president of marketing,</p>
<p>Films for the Humanities and Sciences, based in Princeton, New Jersey, is a wholly owned subsidiary of K-III Education Group.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
